## Finding Text Within Strings

Use `.contains()` to check for a substring, and `.index_of()` to find its position.

### contains — Check for Substring

```xiom
let text = "Hello, World!";
let has_hello = text.contains("Hello");   // true
let has_x = text.contains("X");            // false
let has_world = text.contains("World");    // true
```

### index_of — Find Position

```xiom
let text = "Hello, World!";
let pos = text.index_of("World");  // Some(7)
let nope = text.index_of("xyz");   // None
```

`.index_of()` returns `Option[Int]` — the byte position where the substring starts, or `None`.

### Search Patterns

```xiom
fn has_protocol(url: Str) -> Bool {
  return url.contains("https://") || url.contains("http://");
}

fn find_domain(email: Str) -> Option[Str] {
  let at_pos = email.index_of("@");
  match at_pos {
    Some(pos) => {
      return Some(str_slice(email, pos + 1, email.len()));
    }
    None => { return None; }
  }
}

fn count_occurrences(text: Str, pattern: Str) -> Int {
  var count = 0;
  var pos = text.index_of(pattern);
  while pos.is_some() {
    count = count + 1;
    let start = pos.unwrap_or(0) + pattern.len();
    let rest = str_slice(text, start, text.len());
    pos = rest.index_of(pattern);
  }
  return count;
}
```

### Starts With / Ends With

```xiom
fn starts_with(s: Str, prefix: Str) -> Bool {
  if prefix.len() > s.len() { return false; }
  return str_slice(s, 0, prefix.len()) == prefix;
}

fn ends_with(s: Str, suffix: Str) -> Bool {
  if suffix.len() > s.len() { return false; }
  return str_slice(s, s.len() - suffix.len(), s.len()) == suffix;
}
```

